      },
      "summary": "The change includes pipeline tests for logging and traces, but two explicit acceptance-criterion checks are incomplete: AC-02 does not cover every required sensitive name, and AC-05 does not exercise a formatted-message canary or stack trace.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api.Tests/DiagnosticsTests.cs",
          "line": 129,
          "message": "AC-02's tests do not assert that every listed sensitive name is dropped. Add coverage for omitted names such as `enduser.id`; removing that rule currently leaves the tests passing.",
          "confidence": 0.98,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The AC-02 tests check a subset of sensitive names in the theory and pipeline assertions; neither test checks `enduser.id`.",
            "failureScenario": "If `enduser.id` is removed from `SensitiveKeys`, no test in this change fails, even though AC-02 requires that name to be dropped case-insensitively."
          }
        },
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api.Tests/DiagnosticsTests.cs",
          "line": 251,
          "message": "The AC-05 test does not exercise its required formatted-message canary or a stack trace, so those leaks can be introduced without the test failing.",
          "confidence": 0.99,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The AC-05 test logs the fixed template `Operation failed` and constructs exceptions without throwing them, so it supplies no formatted-message canary and no stack trace.",
            "failureScenario": "If the no-properties path stops clearing `FormattedMessage`, the fixed message remains `Operation failed` and the assertions still pass. The test also cannot detect exported stack-trace details because the exception was never thrown."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
